# Machine-local Claude Code state (sessions, caches, personal overrides) stays
# out of the repo. The shared project settings and the spec-guard hooks are
# tracked deliberately — a gate that every clone has to install by hand is not a
# gate. See docs/spec-guard.md.
.claude/*
!.claude/settings.json
!.claude/hooks/
.claude/settings.local.json

# Build output
/wa
/wad
/dist/
/result

# Test binaries left behind by `go test -cpuprofile=...` (the cpuprofile
# flag suppresses the auto-cleanup that go test normally performs).
# `make pgo-capture` produces these in the repo root.
*.test

# Coverage and test-report artifacts. Every one of these is produced in the
# repo root by a command we tell people to run — CONTRIBUTING.md documents the
# cover.out line as the way to check a change before pushing, `make
# sonar-local` adds test-report.json, and .github/scripts/check-coverage.sh
# writes coverage.txt. Untracked and unignored, they are exactly what a
# `git add -A` sweeps up; one nearly shipped in #314. Issue #318.
cover.out
coverage.txt
test-report.json

# AI development artifacts — kept locally for development reference
# but excluded from the public repo. These files contain internal
# architecture details, rate-limiter thresholds, socket auth model,
# and prompt-injection defenses that constitute attack surface if
# exposed. See git log for the scrub rationale.
CLAUDE.md
HANDOFF.md
.specify/
specs/
docs/research-dossiers/
docs/reliability.md
.sonar-local-token
